{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Protect existing refugees from retrospective settlement rule changes",
        "additional_details": "Many refugees entered the UK legally and claimed asylum immediately because returning home was unsafe. They had no access to resettlement schemes. We believe extending their settlement wait to 20 years would undermine their security, harm their children and prolong uncertainty. Refugees already granted protection should retain the five-year route that applied when they rebuilt their lives in the UK. They should not be penalised for seeking safety, many through lawful entry.",
        "background": "Protect people already granted refugee status from retrospective settlement changes. Preserve their existing five-year route to permanent settlement, and ensure people who entered the UK lawfully before claiming asylum are not penalised for the route they used to reach safety.",
